cation/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[],"created_at":1785384346157635001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"df43e8cd-5cdd-4a52-8648-07416952b5f7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5f6d-7c03-9f3e-4db7"},{"link_uuid":"c7277b15-890c-4926-a221-5896368e87e0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ca69-ba71-8da2-4062"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nplan_review_precheck runs the deterministic floor before the LLM passes, but only a P8 too-big block short-circuits; the code states \"A P1/P5 DET block does NOT stop the LLM\" (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:208-215). A plan that fails the blocking clarity floor (P1) therefore pays the full four-pass LLM review it is guaranteed to fail.\n\n## Approach\nWiden the existing P8 short-circuit branch in plan_review_precheck (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:216-239) from \"P8 blocked\" to \"any DET gate produced a blocking finding\", reusing the same partition_findings/finalize_verdict path so the BLOCK verdict carries the DET findings with coverage.llm_ran=False. No change is needed in src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py: its _degraded_plan_review_verdict outage path already passes ALL det_blocks (not just P8) into partition_findings, confirmed by reading that function. The existing workflow test test_p1_det_block_still_runs_llm_and_blocks (tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py:448) asserts the OLD behavior and is inverted by this change: it will be rewritten to assert finder.calls == 0 and a BLOCK verdict with coverage.llm_ran False. Alternative rejected: adding a content check to claimability.py — that seam is deliberately status-only (no plan-content checks) and reusing it would blur the fast-fail contract.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py, tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py (invert test_p1_det_block_still_runs_llm_and_blocks), tests/unit/workflow/test_det_short_circuit.py (new).\n\n## Testing\nUnit with the workflow test fixtures: a plan with no `## Acceptance Criteria` checklist (P1 block) yields BLOCK with zero finder calls; a DET-passing plan runs the LLM passes exactly as before; the emitted verdict carries the DET blocking findings and standard remediation text.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Any DET-floor blocking finding yields a BLOCK verdict with coverage.llm_ran False and zero finder invocations (checked: rewritten test_p1_det_block_still_runs_llm_and_blocks plus new cases in tests/unit/workflow/test_det_short_circuit.py).\n- [ ] DET-passing plans run the full LLM passes unchanged (checked: existing plan-review workflow tests pass unmodified apart from the one inverted test).\n- [ ] The short-circuit verdict includes every DET blocking finding (checked: unit test asserts finding ids present).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"widen short-circuit branch"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py","reason":"invert P1 short-circuit test"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_det_short_circuit.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"],["relates_to","5f6d-7c03-9f3e-4db7"],["relates_to","ca69-ba71-8da2-4062"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"06670454-988c-4ac5-8532-eb3e76f31943","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"228b-a32b-cdbc-41ca","ticket_type":"story","title":"Short-circuit the plan review before any LLM pass on a DET-floor block","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["190b58a1-d18a-45e5-abcf-c5928ccfeb10","35417e26-25eb-4eef-96a1-5db98ec15be7","246cd83a-dac5-4b3f-989e-f40607de9cf7","a3b1eaef-f5d6-47ca-ae2d-3b663f59f286","bac9ab39-e83c-47e7-8b2c-e0d7e5bcffb4","06670454-988c-4ac5-8532-eb3e76f31943","6a3fa4e2-62a9-49d8-9ef0-9e35c837d96a","890153f1-6847-4ee4-bf83-0518fef6e681","df43e8cd-5cdd-4a52-8648-07416952b5f7","c7277b15-890c-4926-a221-5896368e87e0"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785399266753800102,"uuid":"bf9cf053-3768-4a16-a5a1-5a8bdbb12c7e"}